{"seq":11,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-none-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:20:29.263Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"cfa383891b38f30bfd3f550e6200b4ae6ae82b68887c4aeffbca80aa344c34d3","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"@Bettina Kroll, here's the Pellucid Harbor Logistics and Driftmoor Marine Freight list from #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's four Coastal digests. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)**\n- **#4419**: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. Still open (Moss's Coastal cheat sheet).\n- **Chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change**: the main friction point. No ticket number in these sources (cheat sheet).\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)**\n- **Feature request #882**: a bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by warehouse managers (cheat sheet).\n- **Tide-table import macro failure on Terminal B**: engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. No ticket number given (cheat sheet).\n- **Patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift**: requested by DMF (Moss's 2 Nov digest). The sources don't record its status.\n\n**Conflict to check:** Moss's 2 Nov digest lists **#4419** as \"barge slip 7 schedule sync\" under Kwame's port account. The cheat sheet has the same number for the PHL yard-dwell report. Please confirm which account #4419 belongs to before Kwame's review uses it.\n\nI left out the PD-4821, PD-4824, PD-4827 and #8812 tickets, which belong to Pellow Home Living and Saltmarsh Provisions. The channel messages had no other PHL or DMF tickets."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
